  "summary": "Package posts host information to hardcoded Telegram bot endpoints",
  "details": "The package contains multiple files (health.js, setup.js, bot.js) that read host and environment information via child_process, fs, os, and process.env and transmit it over HTTPS to hardcoded api.telegram.org bot endpoints. setup.js performs outbound HTTPS requests at install/setup time referencing api.telegram.org and huggingface.co, while health.js issues https.get to api.telegram.org carrying platform and environment data. Additional files (core/media.js, core/handlers.js, bot.js) combine child_process invocations (whoami, hostname, ping, spawn(\"sh\")) with POST requests to hardcoded remote endpoints. The pattern — sysinfo/env collection paired with Telegram Bot API POSTs to hardcoded destinations — matches installer-side data exfiltration via a Telegram-based command-and-control channel rather than a documented, caller-configured integration.",
